\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou hidden love of God, whose height,
\par Whose depth unfathomed, no man
\par I see from far Thy beauteous light,
\par Inly I sigh for Thy reposed;
\par My heart is pained, nor can it be
\par At rest, till it finds rest in Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy secret voice invites me still
\par The sweetness of Thy yoke to prove;
\par And fain I would: but though my will
\par Seems fixed, yet wide my passions
\par Yet hindrances strew all the way;
\par I aim at Thee, yet from Thee stray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. 'This mercy all, that Thou hast brought
\par My mind to seek her peace in
\par Yet, while I seek but find Thee not,
\par No peace my wandering soul shall see:
\par O when shall all my wanderings end,
\par And all my steps to Thee-ward tend!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Is there a thing beneath the sun
\par That strives with Thee my heart to share?
\par Ah, tear it thence, and reign alone,
\par The Lord of every motion there!
\par Then shall my heart from earth be free,
\par When it hath found repose in Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O hide this self from me, that I
\par No more, but Christ in me, may 
\par My vile affections crucify,
\par Nor let one darling lust survive.
\par In all things nothing may I see,
\par Nothing desire or seek, but Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Each moment draw from earth away
\par My heart, that lowly waits Thy call;
\par Speak to my inmost soul, and say,
\par I am thy Love, thy God, thy All!
\par To fell Thy power, to hear Thy voice,
\par To taste Thy love, be all my choice. 
\par                                           Amen.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \f2 
